{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1127000-can-mages-usually-do-magic-tricks-at-party-to-make-money","id":1127000,"title":"Can Mages usually do magic tricks at party to make money.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T23:48:49-07:00","id":1127000,"title":"Can Mages usually do magic tricks at party to make money.","content":"Like can they become a Lance Burton at a birthday party to make some quick money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T00:47:49-07:00","id":1127004,"title":"","content":"If you're doing actual Awakened Magic, the first question I have is how are you interacting with your paradigm to cause the effects to happen? Are you combining Enochian incantations into the performance (Hermetic)? Did you drop acid before going on so your hallucinations could manifest (Ecstatic)? Are you using a hidden antigravity machine (Etherite)?<br /> <br /> You'll need to clarify with your Storyteller their interpretation of Coincidental vs Vulgar and Witnesses vs No Witnesses. My own thinking is that a scenario that gets Sleeper witnesses to dismiss vulgar effects as deceptions causes them to not count as witnesses, BUT does not change a vulgar effect to a coincidental one. To actually turn a vulgar effect into a coincidental one it needs to accepted as real by the Consensus, not accepted as a trick. But your Storyteller may feel differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:02:37-07:00","id":1127013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1127000-can-mages-usually-do-magic-tricks-at-party-to-make-money?p=1127004#post1127004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're doing actual Awakened Magic, the first question I have is how are you interacting with your paradigm to cause the effects to happen? Are you combining Enochian incantations into the performance (Hermetic)? Did you drop acid before going on so your hallucinations could manifest (Ecstatic)? Are you using a hidden antigravity machine (Etherite)?<br /> <br /> You'll need to clarify with your Storyteller their interpretation of Coincidental vs Vulgar and Witnesses vs No Witnesses. My own thinking is that a scenario that gets Sleeper witnesses to dismiss vulgar effects as deceptions causes them to not count as witnesses, BUT does not change a vulgar effect to a coincidental one. To actually turn a vulgar effect into a coincidental one it needs to accepted as real by the Consensus, not accepted as a trick. But your Storyteller may feel differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>da fuk? I was thinking a mage can turn a piece of napkin into a pigeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:05:13-07:00","id":1127014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1127000-can-mages-usually-do-magic-tricks-at-party-to-make-money?p=1127013#post1127013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> da fuk? I was thinking a mage can turn a piece of napkin into a pigeon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As in with Awakened Magic, or just doing a Sleeper magic trick? Because if it's the former, creating new life from the inanimate is a pretty powerful vulgar spell to use so casually in front of Sleepers. There are way less high-paradox-risk ways to make money.<br /> <br /> If you mean actually just use slight of hand - yeah, sure whatever. You could probably even use Mind or Time or Correspondence to grease your tricks coincidentally. You'd still need to do the slight of hand, but the actual magic could make it easier/more perfectly executed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-10-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:29:57-07:00","id":1127043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1127000-can-mages-usually-do-magic-tricks-at-party-to-make-money?p=1127013#post1127013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> da fuk? I was thinking a mage can turn a piece of napkin into a pigeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to read a book or something.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T05:08:43-07:00","id":1127053,"title":"","content":"Best case: It wouldn't be too hard to aport in a pigeon under napkin and not worry too much about it. It's just Correspondence 2. So, a Hermetic doing a &quot;say the magic word&quot;, draw upon the Mythic Thread of &quot;Stage Magician Tricks&quot;. It's Coincidental if there's such a thing as such a Mythic Thread. So, Diff. 5. Add in a few factors to reduce Diff to the min. of 3. Assume an Arete of 3. It's got a really good chance of working and a significantly good chance of not blowing up in your face. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, this could easily be a way to make a few bucks, get into that highly secured mansion as a performer at the resident kid's birthday party, etc. Though it could still blow up in your face. I<br /> <br /> Worst case: A pigeon, either from nothing or from a napkin is going to take an Adept with Life 4 to start with. Considering what such a person is capable of doing, this must be for fun or some sort of weird obligation (like a geas or as payment for a debt or on a dare...) because they could be doing really really significant things and probably don't require payment. (For what? Food? They can make pigeons and apple trees. And not need to eat very often. And... And...). But it's almost certainly Vulgar. Thank the powers for the napkin, so there are no Witnesses. But that's Diff. 8 to start with and an allowable reduction to Diff. 5. And only 4 dice to roll. So it's going to work a bit more than 1/2 the time in a single roll at the cost of 1 Paradox per. Your pigeon making limit needs to be pretty low to avoid consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:06:28-07:00","id":1127096,"title":"","content":"Indeed, it's harder than it's worth. It's better to just do the illusions just as any human would (with tricks).<br /> <br /> However, it has been mentioned that there's a Mythic Thread of &quot;stage magic&quot;. That already reduces the difficulty in 1, and may make Coincident things that otherwise would be Vulgar at ST discretion.Thus, this can be a good way to surprise someone, to ease your magick-of course, you will have to have a way to combine your magic with the Thread.<br /> <br /> On the Paradigm aspect: I think &quot;stage magic&quot; could be an interesting Practice in itself (somewhat along the lines of &quot;gutter magick&quot; and &quot;art of desire&quot; perhaps?. Good for &quot;Everything it's an Illusion&quot; Paradigms).<br /> Even then, it would still pay off to use tricks 99% of the time, reserve your &quot;best tricks&quot; (those that can cheat Reailty itself) for special situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:46:39-07:00","id":1127221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1127000-can-mages-usually-do-magic-tricks-at-party-to-make-money?p=1127043#post1127043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might want to read a book or something.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I want to read a book or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}